course: dictionary
lesson: 11198
title: Withering: dying plants and cutting looks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Withering comes from the verb wither, which means drying up, shrinking and dying. «The plants were withering because nobody had watered them.» The clue is no water: plants need water, so without it they dry up and die.
explain: Withering can also describe a look or a remark. «She gave him a withering look.» The clue is that he felt small and foolish, so a withering look is very scornful and makes someone feel silly.
explain: Withering can also mean extremely strong and damaging, as in «withering heat». Ask yourself what word would fit. Then swap in your meaning, such as "scornful look" or "extremely strong heat", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Withering is a form of the verb wither, which means drying up, shrinking and dying.
fact: A plant that is withering is drying up and dying, often because it has no water or light.
fact: «A withering look» is a very scornful look that makes someone feel small and foolish.
fact: «Withering heat» means extremely strong and damaging heat.
fact: Withering can also be a name with a capital letter: «the doctor William Withering wrote about it in 1785» (the foxglove medicine digitalis). Use the clues to tell which meaning is used.
exercise: «The plants were withering because nobody had watered them.» What was the main cause? | A cold wind | Too much sunshine | *They had no water | Too many flowers
exercise: «She gave him a withering look, and he felt very small.» What does withering mean here? | Wet and grey | Bright and sparkling | Kind and warm | *Very scornful, making him feel small
exercise: «The desert sun brought withering heat, and the grass turned brown.» What does withering suggest? | Cool and pleasant | *Extremely strong and damaging | Funny | Quiet and gentle
test: «The leaves were withering because the plant had no water.» What is the best meaning of withering? | Growing very fast | Glowing in the dark | *Drying up and dying
test: Maya says a withering remark is kind. Why is she wrong? | *It is scornful and makes someone feel small | It is a warm hug | It is a soft whisper | It makes everyone laugh happily
exam: «The ___ look from the teacher made Sam shrink in his seat.» Which word fits best? | Kind | Happy | Sleepy | *Withering
